+| LIMIT | フレームの長さ上限 | 1 (bytes) | LF含む1024bytes | cooperative bounded input | integer scalar |
+| CHUNK | 1回のraw読取上限 | 1 (bytes) | 4096bytes | 有限パイプデータ | integer scalar |
+| u_c | 合成標準不確かさ | s | 今回は未推定 | 校正データなし | unavailable scalar |
+| k | 包含係数 | 1 | 今回は未設定 | u_c未推定 | unavailable scalar |
+
+## Analytical reduction and unit check
+Initially R,F,B are empty. Each successful raw read appends the same returned
+bytes to R and B. Extracting one LF-terminated prefix appends it to F and removes
+exactly that prefix from B. By induction after each operation, R is the
+concatenation of F then B. Thus no collected byte is lost or reordered within
+this single-reader accumulator. EOF with nonempty B is not a full frame. Decoding
+only complete frames allows a UTF-8 code point to span two raw reads.
+
+This invariant does not imply that all frames arrive by a deadline. A selector
+can report readable from a partial prefix; a blocking readline must still wait
+for LF or EOF. Conversely a previous raw read may consume two frames while
+readline returns only the first: the second remains in the library buffer, not
+the now-empty kernel pipe. These two distinct states explain the countercontrols.
+
+The candidate checks an absolute deadline before waiting/reading and validates
+it after decode; nonblocking os.read does not itself wait for a future suffix.
+This cannot bound OS scheduling or arbitrary computation pauses, so the return
+bound is measured rather than claimed proved. Deadline comparisons use ns on
+both sides; subtracting two monotonic timestamps gives a duration. Dividing ns
+by1,000,000 yields ms. Frame counts and concatenation contain no time dimension.
+
+## Roadmap and publication boundary
+R0 exact old-byte audit (no old actors) -> R1 excluded construction -> R2 local
+source/gate freeze -> R3 three first-outcome batches -> R4 raw audit/controls ->
+R5 complete local source/raw/report and additive patch -> R6 GitHub successor,
+qualified PR/CI/main readback when a permitted write operation is available.
+R6 is not inferred from R5. The current connector exposes48 read actions only;
+Plugin directory search locates the already installed GitHub connector, with no
+other authenticated writer. git exists; gh/docker and credential configuration
+are absent, and GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN/GIT_ASKPASS are not set. No credential scan
+or write bypass is attempted. Remote Issue/PR creation is not a pilot prerequisite
+in this explicitly local allocation. Global ROADMAP stays open.
+
+## First local outcome
+
+PASS_LOCAL_BUFFERED_READINESS_BOUNDARY;48 cases,96 actors,2432 audit checks,
+16 effective evidence controls,12 pure units. Six comparator cases miss9
+buffered complete notifications within the200ms budget; three partial-line
+cases return about140ms late. Candidate matches the fixed table. Neither
+policy grants input/retry authority. Full raw bytes and all failures/limits
+are in the additive package; no old scientific rerun.
